                    </div>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3>3. Enhanced Safety Features for Families</h3>
                    <p>
                        Safety is a top priority, especially when traveling with loved ones. SUVs are designed with advanced safety features
                        that provide peace of mind for drivers and passengers alike. These vehicles often come equipped with features like
                        anti-lock braking systems (ABS), electronic stability control (ESC), lane departure warnings, and multiple airbags
                        strategically placed throughout the cabin. Higher seating positions in SUVs also offer improved visibility, allowing
                        drivers to spot potential hazards more easily. Many modern SUVs include child safety locks and other advance features,
                        making them an excellent choice for families with young children.
                    </p>
