            <section class="section">
                <h2>Exploring Davao with SUV Car Rental</h2>
                <p>
                    Davao City and its surrounding regions offer a mix of urban attractions, natural wonders, and cultural experiences that are
                    best explored with the versatility of an SUV. Whether you’re visiting for the first time or planning a local road trip,
                    renting an SUV can enhance your travel experience, providing comfort and reliability for every adventure. Here’s a guide
                    to exploring Davao with an SUV:
                </p>

                <h3>Must-Visit Attractions</h3>
                <ul class="attraction-list">
                    <li>
                        <strong>Mount Apo & Mountain Parks</strong> – Mt Apo, Known as the highest peak in the Philippines, Mount Apo is a
                        haven for hikers and nature lovers. Similarly, Marilog-Buda and Kapatagan, Davao Del Sur, are also exciting to
                        visit with SUV. An SUV makes the journey to its trailheads more
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Eden Nature Park</strong> – Located in the highlands, Eden Nature Park offers stunning views, lush gardens,
                        and family-friendly activities. The winding uphill roads to this destination are best navigated with the power and
                        stability of an SUV.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Davao Crocodile Park</strong> – Perfect for families, this park showcases a variety of wildlife and entertaining
                        shows. Its central location makes it an easy stop during your city tour.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Samal Island</strong> – Just a short ferry ride from Davao City, Samal Island boasts pristine beaches and
                        adventure spots like the Monfort Bat Sanctuary. With an SUV, you can conveniently transport gear for snorkeling,
                        diving, or beach lounging.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Recommended Road Trips</h3>
                <ul class="trip-list">
                    <li>
                        <strong>Davao to Tagum City</strong> – Well-paved highways, vibrant festivals, and
                        the Christ the King Cathedral.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Davao to Mati City</strong> – Scenic coastal drive to Dahican Beach, a
                        favorite for surfers and beach lovers.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Davao to Kapatagan</strong> – Mountain escape with views of Mount Apo and
                        attractions like the Agong House, requiring capable vehicles.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Safety Tips While Driving in Davao</h3>
                <ul class="tips-list">
                    <li><strong>Plan Your Route:</strong> Use reliable navigation and know traffic patterns.</li>
                    <li><strong>Drive Defensively:</strong> Be mindful of pedestrians and motorcycles.</li>
                    <li><strong>Check Your Vehicle:</strong> Inspect tires, brakes, and fluid levels.</li>
                    <li><strong>Prepare for Weather:</strong> Tropical rain can arrive suddenly—drive cautiously.</li>
                    <li><strong>Secure Belongings:</strong> Lock the vehicle and keep valuables out of sight.</li>
                </ul>
